{"context":"- Anvil v2 preserves the four-domain lifecycle model (Project → Artifact → Deployment → Server Runtime) and its one-way dependency rule (ANVIL_V2_TRANSITION_PLAN §1.2, §2.3; ADR-015).\n- The Server Runtime Domain in v1.x accumulated a platform-ambition excess: registry ownership semantics, the shared-links model, and `root:anvil` provisioning ambitions (Review 20 §1, §2.3 item 1).\n- The ownership/provisioning model is philosophically inconsistent with the convention domain; lifecycle state on the server is required by the convention, the ownership model is not (Review 20 §1).\n- The worst defects live in this excess: D2 (dual state path), D3 (One-Active invariant unwired), D4 (adapter phases run after promotion) (ANVIL_V2_TRANSITION_PLAN §3 A9).\n- \"Server Runtime Domain\" (a bounded context)  Source: ADR-031-server-runtime-scope-alignment.md Date:2026-08-03 Status:Proposed.","decision":"- The Server Runtime Domain is scoped to lifecycle state and enforcement: **state, install, activate, rollback, locking**. Locking is carried forward from the v1.x runtime operational contract (ADR-013, ADR-014) — concurrent lifecycle operations on one server require it; the Transition Plan's A9 keep-list (state, install, activate, rollback) does not enumerate it, so this ADR records the source explicitly.\n- The platform-ambition excess is demoted and is NOT part of the v2 runtime: registry ownership semantics, the shared-links model, and `root:anvil` provisioning ambitions (Review 20 §2.3 item 1). Provisioning concerns are deferred to existing tools (Ansible, deployment tools).\n- The observation pillar is preserved: lifecycle state remains persisted, queryable, and authoritative (ANVIL_MA","consequences":"- **Positive:** smaller defect surface; philosophically consistent with the convention domain; provisioning stays external to Anvil.\n- **Positive:** the state-only Server Runtime remains the enforcement and observation surface for install, activate, rollback, and locking.\n- **Negative:** Server Runtime provisioning/ownership surfaces are removed or demoted — a governed breaking change at A9 completion (ANVIL_V2_TRANSITION_PLAN §12.1); operations documentation is revised in Phase 4.\n- **Neutral:** ADR-013's Registry/State separation remains valid within the state-only scope; registry files must never carry operational state.","alternativesConsidered":"Considered\n\n- **Keep the ownership/provisioning model.** Rejected: it is the platform-ambition excess (Review 20 §1), provisioning is not owned by Anvil (ANVIL_MANIFESTO §4.2), and it hosts the worst defects (D2–D4).\n- **Remove the Server Runtime Domain entirely.** Rejected: the observation pillar must survive — lifecycle state stays the persisted, queryable system of record (ANVIL_V2_TRANSITION_PLAN §2.2; ANVIL_MANIFESTO §4.1).\n- **Defer the scope decision until after v2 planning.** Rejected: t"}